												ELASTIC SEARCH (or INVERTED) INDEX
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
In real world, We may need to search substring to find matches and DB indexes wont' work.
Search Index: We Tokenize text.
Eg: Document 1(Id: 69, Value: "Hello, World") and Document 2(Id:45, Value:"Hello There") is stored as

Prefix Search: Soretd Inverted Indexes and we can binary search now. 
 [Hello:45,69]
 [World:69]

Suffix Search : Invert and Sort Prefix Index
[dlroW:69]
[olleH:45,69]

Eg: Lucene is a tech that implements search index (runs on single node)

ELASTIC SEARCH: built on top of Lucene for Distributed System
Similar to Secondary Indexes: We build Search (or inverted) index per partion. For global serach, we may have to join partition.

Partition1 (1-50) : [Hello:20,45 | There:45]. .|||||. .Partition2 (50-100): [Hello:69 | World:69]
Search Hello -> 20,45,69

Caching: We can cache popular search results